  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the retrieval:\n\n**FastAPI request validation chain:**\n- `fastapi/routing.py` \u2014 `get_request_handler`: negotiates Content-Type (checks `request.headers.get(\"content-type\")`, defaults to JSON when the header is absent, only parses form data when `content_type` indicates `multipart/form-data` or `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`), reads raw body, calls `request.json()`, and routes into dependency solving.\n- `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` \u2014 `solve_dependencies`, `request_body_to_args`, `request_params_to_args`: converts the deserialized JSON dict into per-field values, applying `field.validate()` per `ModelField`, filling missing/optional fields with deep-copied defaults, and building structured `loc`-tagged error lists.\n- `fastapi/_compat.py` \u2014 Pydantic v1/v2 compatibility shim; on Pydantic v2 wraps each field in a `TypeAdapter` and calls `validate_python(value, from_attributes=True)`; defines `get_missing_field_error` (produces Pydantic's \"Field required\" / `missing` error when a key is absent \u2014 this is distinct from a key present with `None`).\n- `fastapi/encoders.py` \u2014 `jsonable_encoder`, used for the response side but establishes FastAPI's own semantics for `None`/`exclude_none`/`exclude_unset`, useful as the mirror to httpx's JSON encoding.\n- `fastapi/exceptions.py` \u2014 `RequestValidationError` shape that surfaces as the 422 response.\n\n**httpx request encoding chain:**\n- `httpx/_content.py` \u2014 `encode_request`/`encode_json`/`encode_urlencoded_data`/`encode_multipart_data`: `encode_json` is a bare `json.dumps(json)` with no model-awareness (so `None` fields serialize as JSON `null`, not omitted); `encode_urlencoded_data` (`data=` form path) instead runs every value through `primitive_value_to_str`.\n- `httpx/_utils.py` \u2014 `primitive_value_to_str`: converts `None` \u2192 `\"\"` (empty string) for form-encoded/query data, `True`/`False` \u2192 `\"true\"`/`\"false\"`. This is the sharpest drift point vs. FastAPI's \"missing key\" semantics.\n- `httpx/_models.py` \u2014 `Request.__init__`/`_prepare`: only sets `Content-Type` when going through `encode_request` (i.e., only when `stream=` isn't used directly); auto Content-Length/Transfer-Encoding logic.\n- `httpx/_client.py` \u2014 `build_request`: the actual call site wiring `json=`/`data=`/`content=` into `Request`.\n\nReady to hand this file set to whoever writes `/workspace/analysis/IMPACT_REPORT.md`.",
